From: Arjan van de Ven <arjan@linux.intel.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:51:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Replace libpci with a built-in pci.ids parser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PowerTOP only used libpci for a vendor:device -> name lookup. Parse
pci.ids directly (hwdata, misc and /usr/share locations) instead, which
removes the libpci build dependency, the HAVE_NO_PCI auto-detection and
the permanent libpci leak (valgrind suppression and release-checklist
exception).

HAVE_NO_PCI is now only a test switch that prevents loading the host's
pci.ids; tests feed fixtures through pci_ids_parse(). Also silence a
constant-folded -Wformat-truncation warning in the pt_strcpy test.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/fenrus75/powertop/commit/1f32bb317811230913f37d5461b5ead9a08e325b]
[Sven: only backported the necessary parts. Skipped test and docs]
Signed-off-by: Sven Püschel <s.pueschel@pengutronix.de>
---
 meson.build |  10 -----
 src/lib.cpp | 129 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 src/lib.h   |   3 ++
 3 files changed, 105 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

